00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:22,160
Emotions are an essential and inseparable part of our consciousness.

184
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:26,940
They are part of a built -in mechanism which allows us to cope with the ups and

185
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,720
downs of our lives both physically and mentally.

186
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:35,440
When we hide our emotions and our true feelings, we stop being genuine, spontaneous,

187
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,440
and authentic in our relationships.

188
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:43,080
When we put on cultivated and polished faces in the company of others, we stop being

189
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,200
true to ourselves.

190
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:50,560
Socially, it may be a good tactic to hide our true emotions, but morally it is also

191
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,240
a breach of faith and trust.

192
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:57,980
Although humans are more advanced and intelligent, animals are more genuine and

193
00:18:57,980 --> 00:19:01,680
authentic in their behaviour and responses than human beings.

194
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:06,800
The more educated we are, the less transparent and reliable we become.

195
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:11,040
We are drawn to our pets because pets do not lie.

196
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:16,140
One of the first steps in dealing with emotions such as anger or fear is to

197
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:18,480
acknowledge them as normal and human.

198
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:24,280
There is nothing sinful or immoral about being emotional unless your emotions make

199
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:27,440
you inhuman, insensitive, and cruel to others.

200
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:32,480
Feelings of guilt associated with emotions are more devastating and damaging than

201
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,360
the experience of emotion itself.

202
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:39,800
So when you deal with the problem of emotions, you should learn not only how to

203
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:44,820
control them, but also how to accept them and manage the guilt and anguish arising

204
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:51,700
from them. Our brains are made up of a primitive inner core and a more evolved and

205
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:53,040
rational outer core.

206
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:58,160
Most of the time, the rational part of the mind controls the information coming from

207
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:03,500
the primitive core and makes its own decisions as to what to do and how to respond.

208
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:09,380
However, during critical situations, especially when a threat is perceived, the

209
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:14,140
outer core loses control and fails to regulate the impulses and instinctive

210
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:16,180
responses coming from the primitive brain.

211
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:21,740
As a result, we let disturbing thoughts and emotions arise in our consciousness and

212
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:23,780
surrender to our primitive behaviour.

213
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:30,320
In times of emotional turmoil, remember that emotions arise because your senses are

214
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:36,260
wired to the primitive part of your mind which is self -regulated, autonomous, and

215
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:40,520
Your rational mind does not always deal with the messages coming from it

216
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:45,760
effectively. These messages are part of your survival mechanism and should not be

217
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:50,100
stifled simply because emotions are unhealthy and betray your weaknesses.

218
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:56,100
When emotions arise, instead of stifling them, pay attention to them and try to

219
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:58,640
understand the messages they are trying to deliver.

220
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:03,960
This way, you make use of your emotions without losing your balance and inner

221
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:10,460
stability. Questions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.

